{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1181149-changeling-tier-0-5","id":1181149,"title":"Changeling Tier 0,5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-31T09:00:00-08:00","id":1181149,"title":"Changeling Tier 0,5","content":"While some games in CoD, like Mage, seems created for epic, grand stories of global importance, Changeling strikes me as the extreme opposite: everything seems to be set towards intimate tales directly about your characters. <br /> <br /> I am planning to run a very local campaign. With action taking place in my home city which is well known to all players (a very historic place with less than 500 000 inhabitants in Europe), with Freehold of less than ten Changeling, where every NPC can be really well fleshed out. Everyone will be coming from the same Keeper, so they all have the most personal enemy. I plan to keep the story tightly focused on characters, their Fetches, and their struggle and to reunite with the society with the pertinent presence of their captor.<br /> <br /> Has anyone tried running such a game? Essentialy, everything in CtL seems really set towards such a campaign: you are immediately given one very personal threat and relatively little obvious stuff to do that hasn't anything to do with you personally. I am interested to hear your low-key stories or any advice you can give on running such games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:12:21-08:00